(7310140, 1140230, 163430, '<td valign="top">Cute. Not very photographic, but cute. I cannot decide how to rate the idea, yet. It''s original (good), funny (good), but not very photographic (bad). Setting this aside, there are some things related to the composition and lighting that should have been thought over in more details during the setup:<br/>- I cannot see clearly, but the steering wheel seems to be on the left side. This should imply that the Mini should drive (and park) on the right side of the road.<br/>- The shadow does not match the position of the depicted light source (the sun, the clouds, the time of day). <br/>- A pissed of (or desperate) driver somewhere around the car would be nice, either as a figure or as a drawing. :-) But this is not essential.<br/> <br/> <br/>Haven''t voted yet. This is my first browse of the entries and this was the first image on my list.</td>', 'Cute. Not very photographic, but cute. I cannot decide how to rate the idea, yet. It''s original (good), funny (good), but not very photographic (bad). Setting this aside, there are some things related to the composition and lighting that should have been thought over in more details during the setup:- I cannot see clearly, but the steering wheel seems to be on the left side. This should imply that the Mini should drive (and park) on the right side of the road.- The shadow does not match the position of the depicted light source (the sun, the clouds, the time of day). - A pissed of (or desperate) driver somewhere around the car would be nice, either as a figure or as a drawing. :-) But this is not essential.  Haven''t voted yet. This is my first browse of the entries and this was the first image on my list.', '2015-02-03 18:22:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(7310143, 1140245, 163430, '<td valign="top">Interesting, but under par in some photographic elements:<br/>- I would have went with B&amp;W. The colors do not add to the story and the background is full of blue-purple haze. If not full B&amp;W at least eliminate the distracting colors at the back.<br/>- The tree is, to me, based on the composition, the major element in the shot, not the oil pump. It''s taking over the attention due to the placement and the size. Furthermore, there is no separation between the pump and the tree.</td>', 'Interesting, but under par in some photographic elements:- I would have went with B&W. The colors do not add to the story and the background is full of blue-purple haze. If not full B&W at least eliminate the distracting colors at the back.- The tree is, to me, based on the composition, the major element in the shot, not the oil pump. It''s taking over the attention due to the placement and the size. Furthermore, there is no separation between the pump and the tree.', '2015-02-03 18:23:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(7310145, 1140276, 163430, '<td valign="top">This i have seen before, but i''m not going to hold that against you. :-)<br/>It is certainly original to this challenge. The sharpness is good and the greenish color at the bottom of the background matches the color of the olives. <br/>The lighting is a bit uneven (top to bottom). It looks correctable in post. The camera (or spoon) angle could have been a bit better as well. I see the sides of the top two spoons bu the inside of the third.<br/>I cannot decide whether it needs a bit more color vibrance (or saturation) or not.</td>', 'This i have seen before, but i''m not going to hold that against you. :-)It is certainly original to this challenge. The sharpness is good and the greenish color at the bottom of the background matches the color of the olives. The lighting is a bit uneven (top to bottom). It looks correctable in post. The camera (or spoon) angle could have been a bit better as well. I see the sides of the top two spoons bu the inside of the third.I cannot decide whether it needs a bit more color vibrance (or saturation) or not.', '2015-02-03 18:25:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(7310216, 1140482, 109227, '<td valign="top">Great image; one of my top picks.</td>', 'Great image; one of my top picks.', '2015-02-03 19:25:35.000000', NULL, 1),
